AUDIO: 'So today we\'re talking all about dash cams. I went&nbsp; out and I purchased multiple different dash cams&nbsp;&nbsp; from multiple manufacturers to try and see is&nbsp; there really any difference between a $100 dash&nbsp;&nbsp; cam, a $250 dash cam, and like a $400 dash cam.&nbsp; So in this video, I\'ve got four dash cameras from&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Vofo. I\'ve got four dash cameras from Thinkware.&nbsp; I\'ve got three dash cameras from Garmin. And just&nbsp;&nbsp; as a wild card, I added this is the most popular&nbsp; dash cam on Amazon. It retails for about 100&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bucks. It\'s made by a company called Rove. So,&nbsp; we\'re going to see how all of these dash cams&nbsp;&nbsp; first of all compare to one another. We\'re going&nbsp; to see is there really really any major difference&nbsp;&nbsp; between all these different brands. And then we\'re&nbsp; also going to be able to see, okay, if you spend&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a h 100red bucks or you spend 400 bucks, what&nbsp; does that actually look like in terms of usable&nbsp;&nbsp; footage here? So, with all that, let me bring you&nbsp; guys over to the bench and kind of go over some&nbsp;&nbsp; of the details of what exactly I have here. All&nbsp; right, so over here at the bench, I\'ve got all of&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the cameras sort of laid out here so we can see&nbsp; exactly what I purchased here. So, starting out&nbsp;&nbsp; down here on the left, I\'ve got three options&nbsp; from Garmin. I\'ve got this option from Rove,&nbsp;&nbsp; which includes a rear camera. This is the most&nbsp; popular camera that you can buy on Amazon. I want&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:20] [scene:talk]
